    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Most box failures are not box failures — they are tape failures. The carton holds, but the seam splits open in transit because someone reached for the cheapest 35-micron BOPP roll for a 20kg double-wall shipment. Understanding what is actually printed on the side of a tape roll — micron, adhesive type, backing material — is the difference between confident shipping and hoping for the best. This guide decodes Malaysian packaging tape standards.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">The Four Tape Families</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">BOPP / OPP (Plastic)</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Biaxially-oriented polypropylene — the everyday e-commerce tape. Available in clear, brown (kraft-coloured), and printed custom variants. Pressure-sensitive adhesive applies in seconds with no water needed. The tape of choice for 90% of Shopee/Lazada sellers, courier parcels, and warehouse pick-and-pack operations. Cheap, fast, reliable for parcels under 15kg.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Kraft Paper Tape</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Pressure-sensitive adhesive on a paper backing. Looks premium against kraft-brown boxes, fully recyclable as paper, and softer aesthetic for craft, food, and lifestyle brands. Adhesion is slightly less aggressive than BOPP — suits boxes that won't see brutal handling, like locally-delivered hampers and gift boxes. Increasingly popular as brands pivot toward fully recyclable mono-material packaging.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Water-Activated Tape (Gummed)</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Paper tape with a starch-based glue that activates with water — applied via a dispensing machine that wets the tape just before it lays down. Within 30 seconds it bonds chemically with the carton's kraft fibres. The result is tamper-evident, premium-looking, and forms a permanent seal that cannot be quietly opened. Used by Apple, premium D2C brands, and Malaysian cosmetics subscriptions for the unboxing experience.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Reinforced / Fibreglass Tape</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Either BOPP or kraft backing with embedded fibreglass or polyester strands. The strands prevent the tape splitting along its length under sustained load. Used for boxes over 15kg, pallet wrapping, and any shipment going through multi-handling international transit. The strands are visible as faint lines through the tape backing.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Reading the Tape Spec</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Width × Length × Micron</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Standard BOPP comes in 48mm × 100m × 45 micron. The width is your sealing capacity — 48mm covers a typical box flap with one strip; 72mm wide for big cartons. Length is roll yield — 100m roughly 100 boxes worth of seal. Micron is thickness, and the most under-appreciated number on the spec sheet — 45 micron is fine for under 5kg, 50-55 for typical parcels, 60+ for heavy duty.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Adhesive Type</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Acrylic adhesive — the standard, holds bond from 0°C to 65°C, suits Malaysian climate. Hot-melt rubber — slightly stronger initial tack, but degrades faster in tropical heat (avoid for long-term storage). Solvent-based — strongest bond, used for industrial applications, but more expensive and increasingly being phased out for environmental reasons.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Custom Print on Tape</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Custom-printed tape (logo, brand name, anti-tamper warnings) is a high-leverage branding option. Per-roll cost increases 30-50% above plain tape, but every box you ship becomes a moving billboard. Most printers need 36-72 rolls minimum order. We arrange custom print on BOPP, kraft, and water-activated for Quinocycle wholesale customers.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">When to Pay for the Premium Tape</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Light e-commerce, local courier, parcels under 5kg — 45 micron BOPP is fine and cheap. Heavy or bulky shipments, international air freight, pallet-stacked storage — step up to 50-60 micron or reinforced tape; the saving on damage claims pays for the upgrade many times over. Premium brand experience, subscription unboxing, food and gift packaging — water-activated tape on kraft boxes is the killer combination, and customers feel the difference instantly.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="bg-surface-variant/50 border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-8 my-12">
